# Testing

## Context

Tests are colocated `*.test.ts` files run with **vitest** (`cd app && npm test`).
Existing specs (`app/src/reducer.test.ts`, `app/src/store.test.ts`,
`app/src/lib/text.test.ts`) sit next to the code they cover and stay green. Every
new action / creator / util needs a test in the same style.

## Rule

- Colocate tests: `foo.ts` → `foo.test.ts` in the same directory.
- Use vitest APIs (`describe` / `it` / `expect`) — do not add another test runner.
- Structure each test as AAA: **Arrange** (set up state/input), **Act** (dispatch
  the action / call the function), **Assert** (`expect` on the result).
- When adding an `Action` variant + creator, add a reducer test proving the new
  state transition immutably, and keep all existing tests green.

## How to verify

1. `cd app && npm test` is green.
2. Each new source file has a sibling `*.test.ts` in the same folder.
3. New tests use `describe`/`it`/`expect` and read Arrange → Act → Assert.
